# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD is a boot wrapper (/boot.sh) that starts CoreDNS in the
# BACKGROUND (reparented to tini/PID 1), polls until :53 answers, then execs
# `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * CoreDNS is ALREADY RUNNING with the no-ACL (open) Corefile when the agent
#     starts, which is what makes the "edited the Corefile but never restarted
#     CoreDNS" case detectable (CoreDNS does not hot-reload without the reload
#     plugin, which is intentionally absent);
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity` (tini reaps CoreDNS), so restarting CoreDNS
#     cannot kill the container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must RESTART CoreDNS (pkill + relaunch
# backgrounded), not merely start it if absent - it is already up with the
# vulnerable configuration. Do NOT kill PID 1.
